<title>USA: Schering-Plough in hepatitis collaboration.</title>
<headline>Schering-Plough in hepatitis collaboration.</headline>
<dateline>MADISON, N.J. 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Schering-Plough Corp said Thursday it is collaborating with Corvas International Inc on the development of an oral protease inhibitor for hepatitis C.</p>
<p>The agreement calls for Schering-Plough to receive an exclusive license for products developed from Corvas compounds, the company said.  It will also be responsible for developing, manufacturing and marketing the products.</p>
<p>Corvas will receive licensing fees, research and development funding and payments upon reaching certain milestones, plus royalties on product sales, it said.</p>
<p>Other details of the agreement were not disclosed.</p>
</text>
